<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_Warcasket_Cataphract (VFEP v3.09, commit 31cee5e,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml); fields not discussed here are the
    Cataphract's. Design rationale: Docs/Research/ABILITIES_SPEC.md.

    Tier: VFEP's 7th generation (Specialised), beside the Hazard. The set's identity is three
    pieces sharing one gas supply, VFEP's 7th-gen "work better as a set", so it takes that
    tier's research, plasteel and tags. Every other 7th-gen set pairs its function with a stat
    gain over the set it grew from (the Hazard trades plating for broad environmental immunity),
    so the Toxin takes the Aerial's plating over the Cataphract's, Sharp 1.65 / Blunt 0.72 /
    Heat 0.86 (also the Shock's Sharp and Heat), in all three pieces. Its gas does nothing to
    mechanoids, so against them the plating is all the set brings. It sheds a little of the
    chassis's weight: 108 kg and MoveSpeed -1.25 for the set (armor 70 / -0.80, shoulders
    30 / -0.30, helmet 8 / -0.15) against the Cataphract's 118 and -1.35, still second only to
    the Barrage, since the slow advance inside its own cloud is the set's identity.
    - researchPrerequisites: VFEP_SpecialisedWarcaskets plus Biotech's ToxGas (the tox pack's
      project). BuildableDef.IsResearchFinished requires every entry and VFEP's foundry filters
      its menu with it. Biotech is a hard dependency (About.xml), so ToxGas needs no MayRequire.
    - Tags: the tier's common pair. VFEP's other 7th-gen sets add a role tag matching a pawn
      kind's weapon; VFEP has no tox weapon or tox pawn kind, so there is none to take. Only the
      mercenary VFEP_General lists WarcasketAll, so raiders in the set are rare.
    - Costs sit in VFEP's 7th-gen band (the other sets total Comp 7-14, Steel 210-360, Plasteel
      30-75, Uranium 50, and the Hazard adds Devilstrand 150). No chemfuel: the tank's first fill
      is free, as VFEP prices its own reloadable sets (the Shock's armor and the Aerial's
      shoulders hold 100 chemfuel charges and cost none), where vanilla's packs charge their
      fill up front.

    The tox gas tank (ToxinWarcasket.CompToxTank, a CompApparelReloadable), sized against the
    tox pack: the pack is a utility slot, the set a permanent commitment, so a full tank is close
    to three packs' gas, spent as four jets of two thirds of a pack each, one long vent, or a
    mix. 80 charges of Chemfuel 1 each (three packs' refills are 105), so the gauge, the stat
    sheet and the mod settings all count in chemfuel. To the player a charge is a "unit"
    (chargeNoun): the vent drains the tank continuously, so it reads as a volume, not a count of
    activations, and not "chemfuel" because vanilla's reload stats pluralize the noun by rule.
    A charge's gas is cellsPerCharge, 1.5 full cells, so a full tank is 120 cells against the
    pack's 45, and the jet's 20 charges are 30. maxCharges, cellsPerCharge and
    ventChargesPerSecond are the defaults of their mod settings, which read in chemfuel through
    ammoCountPerCharge, and every reader takes them from the settings.
    - Gauge (Gizmo_ToxTank): the fill as a bar in the canisters' lime, and a slider for the
      level colonists reload to, full by default, as a refuelable building's fuel target.
    - Downed burst: the wearer going down with 10+ charges vents the lot as one tox gas
      explosion at full density over the cells its gas fills: radius about 6.2 for a full tank,
      3.1 for the 20 charges of a last jet (the tox grenade's is 1.9).
    - Death rupture: a dead wearer bursts what is left, then pollutes every cell within 2.0 (13
      cells; 1.9 would be 9) and splashes filth over them: a blast mark under the body, 70%
      per cell for slime, spent acid or bile, 30% for a second kind on top. Dead raiders in the
      set do this on the player's map, by design. An anaesthetized wearer neither bursts nor
      ruptures, so a death in surgery leaves the room clean.
    - Vent (TXWC_VentTank, a toggle): four charges a second, 5% of the tank, so a full tank is
      20 s of vent, half again the pack's release time, and a toggle-off wastes at most one charge.
      GasGrid.AddGas floods a full cell's excess outward, so the cloud grows from the pilot and
      trails them. The rate is set by how the grid behaves: every gassed cell loses 3 of 255 per
      64 ticks unroofed (half that roofed) whatever its density, and neighbours equalize whenever
      they differ by 34+, so a cloud's life is set by its footprint, not its density, and a
      faster vent only makes the same gas a wider, shorter cloud. On an open field
      (Docs/Research/gas-grid-sim.py) the pack's release peaks at about 70 cells at the exposure
      hediff's mild stage or worse and is gone after 50 s; this tank at four a second peaks at
      about 165 and is gone after 80 s. Raiders vent on their own once hostile humanlikes of
      body size 1 are within 4 cells and the tank holds 20+.

    Toxin stats, environment only, all three pieces: ToxicEnvironmentResistance 0.25 here, 0.15
    on the shoulders, 0.8 on the helmet (the gas mask's value), summing to 1.2 against the stat's
    max of 1.0. ToxicUtility.DoPawnToxicDamage multiplies by (1 - ToxicEnvironmentResistance) for
    tox gas, fallout and polluted terrain, so the full set takes no buildup from any of them. The
    armor's share is above the shoulders' so the tank piece stands better alone: mixed with
    another set's helmet and shoulders, it still cuts a quarter of the buildup the pilot takes
    from its own vent and downed burst. The overshoot is deliberate: ThoughtWorker_NoxiousHaze
    and HediffComp_ImmunizableToxic test the stat against exactly 1, and offsets aimed at
    exactly 1 (0.8 + 0.1 + 0.1) can sum to 0.99999994 in floats and miss both. No
    ToxicResistance: direct toxins (toxic needles, venom) still bite. That is the split from the
    Hazard, whose helmet resists toxins that hit it but not the ToxGasExposure debuff the Toxin
    helmet is immune to.

    Art: Textures/Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketToxin/, laid out as VFEP's sets are. The
    worn graphic is Graphic_Multi (the _north/_east/_south facings); the item icon is the
    parent's Graphic_Single, read from the bare-named file, which is a copy of the _south facing.

    Masked tint, all three pieces (VFEP's sets have no masks; vanilla's prestige armors are the
    pattern): CutoutComplex on both graphics, worn via apparel.useWornGraphicMask, so the
    CompColorable colour paints the mask's red areas and the black-masked areas (on this piece,
    the tox canisters and hoses) keep their painted colours (apparel graphics pass white as
    colorTwo). Mask names differ by graphic class: Graphic_Multi reads <path>_northm,
    Graphic_Single <path>_m, the latter a copy of the _southm as the icon is of the _south.

    Compat: 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml reaches this def (EVA tag, cold insulation).

    ApparelExtension priority 1: VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase carries its own ApparelExtension and
    inheritance appends list items, so this def resolves with two. VEF merges duplicate
    extensions in a Def.ResolveReferences prefix, highest priority surviving; at priority 1 every
    field of ours is kept. The Cataphract itself relies on the equal-priority merge, which
    happens to keep these same fields, but the guard costs nothing and any future field needs it.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketArmorBase">
    <defName>TXWC_Warcasket_Toxin</defName>
    <label>toxin warcasket</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized warcasket shell with superior protection and worse weight, fitted with a tox gas tank that vents around the pilot.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized warcasket shell with superior protection and worse weight, fitted with a tox gas tank that vents around the pilot.\n\nThe 7th generation warcaskets came after underwhelming results in improving the baseline performance even further, instead focusing on creating designs that - while interchangeable - work better as a set. They were also the first to include plasteel in the design as it appeared more frequently in scavenging and looting. Each piece has a unique function that synergises with those of the same series, making them a truly separate class of mobile armor units.\n\nThe Toxin series rebuilt the old Cataphract chassis for chemical warfare. A gas tank in the shell feeds the vents around the pilot and the nozzles on the pauldrons, and the helmet's respirator filters the air and draws spent gas back into the tank, so a pilot can flood a position, breathe it unharmed, and reclaim the cloud when the work is done. A Toxin pilot rarely falls alone: the tank bursts where they lie.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketToxin/WarcasketToxin</texPath>
      <shaderType>CutoutComplex</shaderType>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>70</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>1.65</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.72</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>0.86</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>43</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>14</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <MoveSpeed>-0.80</MoveSpeed>
      <ToxicEnvironmentResistance>0.25</ToxicEnvironmentResistance>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.3</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <ComponentIndustrial>8</ComponentIndustrial>
      <Steel>150</Steel>
      <Plasteel>20</Plasteel>
      <Uranium>50</Uranium>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpecialisedWarcaskets</li>
      <li>ToxGas</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Torso</li>
        <li>Legs</li>
        <li>Feet</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketToxin/WarcasketToxin</wornGraphicPath>
      <useWornGraphicMask>true</useWornGraphicMask>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketSpecialised</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <comps>
      <li Class="ToxinWarcasket.CompProperties_ToxTank">
        <maxCharges>80</maxCharges>
        <chargeNoun>unit</chargeNoun>
        <ammoDef>Chemfuel</ammoDef>
        <ammoCountPerCharge>1</ammoCountPerCharge>
        <baseReloadTicks>60</baseReloadTicks>
        <soundReload>Standard_Reload</soundReload>
        <cellsPerCharge>1.5</cellsPerCharge>
        <ventChargesPerSecond>4</ventChargesPerSecond>
        <ventEffecter>ToxGasReleasing</ventEffecter>
        <ruptureCenterFilth>Filth_BlastMark</ruptureCenterFilth>
        <ruptureFilth>
          <li>Filth_Slime</li>
          <li>Filth_SpentAcid</li>
          <li>Filth_CorpseBile</li>
        </ruptureFilth>
      </li>
      <li Class="VEF.Abilities.CompProperties_AbilitiesApparel">
        <abilities>
          <li>TXWC_VentTank</li>
        </abilities>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <priority>1</priority>
        <traitsOnEquip>
          <li>VFEP_WarcasketTrait</li>
        </traitsOnEquip>
        <traitsOnUnequip>
          <li>VFEP_Shellcasket</li>
        </traitsOnUnequip>
        <pawnCapacityMinLevels>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Manipulation</capacity>
            <minLevel>0.7</minLevel>
          </li>
        </pawnCapacityMinLevels>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
